---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import SideNav from '../components/SideNav.astro';
import Showcase from '../components/Showcase.astro';
import CostTable from '../components/CostTable.astro';
import Boundary from '../components/Boundary.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import processorReference from '../generated/processors-reference.json';
import { DOCS_URL, EVIDENCE_URL, QUICKSTART_URL } from '../config';

const builtInProcessors = processorReference.processors;
---
<Base
  title="Inside leani — processors, storage, and the RPC subset"
  description="What leani's processors make of each block, what a node keeps on disk, and exactly which Ethereum JSON-RPC methods it answers."
>
  <Header slot="before-main" />
  <SideNav items={[['#processors', 'processors'], ['#storage', 'storage'], ['#rpc', 'rpc subset']]} />
  <section class="intro wrap" aria-labelledby="inside-h">
    <h1 id="inside-h">Inside leani</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      What processors make of each block, what a node keeps on disk, and
      exactly which Ethereum RPC methods it answers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="processors" class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="processors-h">
    <h2 id="processors-h"><span class="mono"># </span>Processors do the work</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      A processor is a deterministic map/reduce over blocks, transactions,
      receipts, and logs. Configure a built-in, or write your own in Rust or
      Wasm. Each example shows a configuration, the data it extracts, and the
      change stream your app reads.
    </p>
    <Showcase />
    <div class="catalog" aria-label="Built-in processors">
      <span class="mono">{builtInProcessors.length} built in</span>
      {builtInProcessors.map((processor) => (
        <a href={`/docs/reference/processors/#${processor.id}`}>{processor.id}</a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="storage" class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="storage-h">
    <h2 id="storage-h"><span class="mono"># </span>Storage is a policy, not a promise</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      State, query output, delivery, artifacts, checkpoints, undo, and raw
      history have independent lifecycle controls and hard budgets. Keep a
      current value, a rolling window, a reusable history, or only an
      acknowledged external copy.
    </p>
    <CostTable />
    <p class="links">
      <a href={EVIDENCE_URL}>Reproduce the Mainnet evidence gate →</a>
      <a href="/docs/guides/choose-operating-profile/">Choose an operating profile →</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="rpc" class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="rpc-h">
    <h2 id="rpc-h"><span class="mono"># </span>An exact, capability-reported RPC subset</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Existing Ethereum clients can use the block, transaction, receipt, log,
      chain-metadata, and subscription methods leani advertises. Availability
      still depends on configured sources, retained material, and hash locators.
    </p>
    <Boundary />
    <p class="foot">
      Number and range lookups can use historical sources; lookups by hash
      alone cover recent blocks unless a locator or retained index is enabled.
      With no EVM and no state trie, stateful methods fail explicitly instead
      of returning something almost right, so keep an execution provider for
      them. Every method’s behavior is in <a href="/docs/reference/ethereum-json-rpc/">Ethereum JSON-RPC compatibility</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="next wrap">
    Next: the <a href={QUICKSTART_URL}>quickstart</a>, or the <a href={DOCS_URL}>docs</a>.
  </p>
  <Footer slot="after-main" />
</Base>

<style>
  .intro { padding-block: 4.5rem 0; }
  .intro h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5.5vw, 3.6rem); }
  .sub { color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 1.1rem; max-width: 46ch; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .intro + .section { padding-top: 4rem; }
  .lede { margin-bottom: 2.25rem; }
  .catalog { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.45rem; align-items: center; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .catalog span { color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 0.72rem; margin-right: 0.25rem; }
  .catalog a {
    border: 1px solid var(--panel-edge); border-radius: 999px; color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; padding: 0.18rem 0.48rem; text-decoration: none;
  }
  .catalog a:hover { border-color: var(--accent-dim); color: var(--accent); }
  .links { display: flex; gap: 1.25rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.25rem; font-size: 0.88rem; }
  .foot { color: var(--ink-dim); max-width: 62ch; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .next { color: var(--ink-dim); padding-bottom: 6rem; }
</style>
